5,1,1,talk,Servas,,"Welcome, everyone. Let us approach this selection with a spirit of growth. To ensure we build upon our history rather than repeating it, I wish to see the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I agree. I think it would be helpful to see the capital budget and software allowance too, just to be sure we know what we can actually afford.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I want to know about the network coverage at customer plants! And maybe the in-house developer availability too? I bet there are some interesting mysteries hidden in those reports!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I believe we need to focus on the actual operational losses. I will look into the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs and the time lost to copying existing records.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Ryuji that operational efficiency is key. I will look into the staffing of the coordination group and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts to see how we are actually managing our resources.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to look at the present, but we must also understand the path we have walked. To complement the rollout outcomes, I shall also examine the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I guess I should also check the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. I'm worried about how the costs might change later on, so that seems important.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"Actually, I've changed my mind! I want to see the handling of vendor queries too. I wonder if they're getting grumpy because we're not answering them fast enough! Hehe!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,I will stick with my initial choices. Understanding the specific failures in delivery and the inefficiency of manual data entry is the only way to identify where the real problems lie.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,I will maintain my choices. Understanding the current staffing levels and standardization efforts is essential to determine if we have the actual capacity to implement any new proposal without overworking the staff.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see such diverse perspectives. By looking at both our past successes and our current struggles, we shall find a path that serves the whole company. I am content with my selections.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think I'm okay with my choices too. I just want to make sure we don't run into any unexpected costs later. I'll stick with the budget and the vendor pricing.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm all set too! Network coverage and vendor queries it is! I can't wait to see what's going on out there. This is going to be like a treasure hunt! Hehe!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am also satisfied. Focusing on the incident logs and time loss provides the empirical data necessary to avoid making a decision based on superficial appeal. I will wait for the results.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Asuka,,I am also satisfied. My focus remains on the human resource capacity and standardization. We cannot approve a project if the operational foundation is too fragile to support it. I await the findings.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us move forward with a peaceful heart. We have cast a wide net of inquiry, and I trust that the truth revealed in these reports will guide us toward a wise decision.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
