40,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The patterns of the past speak clearly. It seems that tools requiring universal daily effort fade away, while specialized, focused solutions endure. We must seek a proposal that is sustainable and truly useful.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found out that the capital budget is frozen, but there's some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses get more expensive as we expand, while fixed fees are more stable. I'm... a bit worried about that.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, you guys! I found some real mysteries! Some customer plants lose their signal for whole afternoons, and getting device approval takes forever! Also, our poor clerks are asking for the same certificates over and over! Hehe!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data confirms my concerns. We are losing nearly two hours daily to redundant data entry, and misrouted deliveries are caused by inconsistent records, not human error. We must prioritize a solution that addresses these systemic inefficiencies.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data is concerning. The coordination group is severely understaffed, with two people handling everything manually. Furthermore, most standardization efforts have failed due to a lack of ownership. We cannot afford a proposal that adds more unmanaged work.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, @Ryuji, your findings align with what I have seen. When we ask too much of an understaffed team or demand universal daily effort, the project withers. We must choose a focused, sustainable solution.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I agree. Since the capital budget is frozen, we really have to be careful. If we pick something with per-head licenses, the costs might just keep growing and become a problem later.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that sounds scary! But wait, if the plants have no signal and it takes six weeks just to get a device approved, won't any new fancy software just get stuck? We have to check that first! Hehe!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, you are correct. If the infrastructure is failing, a ""fancy"" solution is useless. However, the priority must be fixing the systemic data duplication and record inconsistency that is already costing us hours every single day.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree that systemic inefficiency is a priority, but we must be careful. If the coordination group is already failing to refill posts, any ""fix"" that requires manual oversight will only break the people involved.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance, is it not? We must heal the systemic wounds @Ryuji mentions, yet do so without breaking the spirits of those @Asuka protects. A small, focused light is often more enduring than a great fire.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should look for something that uses the software allowance instead of the capital budget. And maybe something with a fixed fee, so we don't get a huge bill next year. Does that make sense?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"It makes total sense, @Daisuke! But we also can't forget about the signal ghosts! If the software needs the internet to work, it'll just be a fancy paperweight at the plants! We need something that actually works on-site! Hehe!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, that is a valid point. We need a solution that functions offline or handles intermittent connectivity. However, the core requirement remains: it must eliminate the redundant data entry and record conflicts I discovered. Efficiency cannot be an afterthought.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, efficiency is not an afterthought, but it cannot be achieved through more manual labor. We need a solution that is automated and requires minimal administrative overhead, otherwise we are just shifting the burden.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have reached a shared understanding. We seek a solution that is focused, automated, and resilient to poor connectivity, all while remaining fiscally stable. Let us now see which proposal best embodies these virtues.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope the candidates fit those criteria. I'm still really worried about the budget, so I'll be looking closely at the cost structure of the proposals. I'm ready to see them.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Sakura,,Me too! I hope there's a proposal that can beat the signal ghosts and help the clerks! This is getting really exciting! I'm ready to see the candidates! Hehe!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I am ready. We have established the necessary criteria based on empirical evidence. Now we must ensure we select the proposal that solves the actual problems on the floor, not the one that sounds most impressive.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I am also ready. Let us be vigilant; we must ensure the chosen proposal does not simply create a new, invisible workload for an already exhausted staff. I await the candidates.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
