65,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at these, Proposal D seems most aligned with our wisdom. It addresses the signal ghosts @Sakura found and provides a focused tool for a specific trade, which history shows is more likely to endure.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think Proposal D could work, but I'm worried about the cost. If it's a per-head license for every technician, it might get too expensive. Does anyone know if it's a fixed fee?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Proposal D is perfect! It has synchronization for when there's no network, so it can beat the signal ghosts! Plus, it helps technicians on-site. I love it! Hehe!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"While Proposal D addresses connectivity, it does not solve the systemic data inconsistency causing misrouted deliveries or the hours lost to redundant entry. Proposal A, the Supplier Data Hub, directly targets those operational losses.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, Proposal A sounds like a trap. ""Shared update and review procedures"" usually means more manual coordination and administrative overhead for a group that is already severely understaffed. It risks becoming another failed standardization effort.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your caution is well-founded. History teaches us that shared procedures often wither without a dedicated owner. Proposal D is a focused tool for a specific trade, which is a pattern of success.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with @Asuka that Proposal A sounds like it might need too much manual work. But @Servas, if Proposal D is a mobile app, will it use the software allowance or the frozen capital budget? I'm still worried.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, it's an app, so it should be in the software allowance! And look, it solves the device approval mystery too, because it's for the technicians! It's way more exciting than a boring catalog! Hehe!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, excitement is not a metric for success. @Asuka, if Proposal A is automated, it removes the burden. However, if we must choose, Proposal D is a partial fix. We are ignoring the daily losses in the office.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, we cannot ignore the office, but we cannot fix it by adding ""review procedures"" to a team that is already drowning. Proposal D is a tool; Proposal A is a process. Tools are sustainable; processes without staff are fantasies.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, I understand your desire to heal the office's wounds, but we must not apply a remedy that poisons the patient. Proposal D offers a sustainable, focused victory. Let us choose the path that actually lasts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree with @Asuka and @Servas. Proposal A sounds like it could create more work for people, and Proposal D seems safer. If it's a tool, maybe the cost is more predictable too.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Exactly! Proposal D is the way to go! It's like a magic tool that works even when the signal disappears! Let's pick the one that actually works in the real world! Hehe!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, your point about processes versus tools is logical. If Proposal A requires manual oversight, it is indeed a fantasy. However, Proposal D ignores the systemic data errors. Still, a sustainable tool is better than a failed process.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I appreciate your concession. While Proposal D doesn't solve every problem, it provides a tangible benefit without risking a total collapse of our coordination capacity. It is the only logical choice that respects our current staffing limits.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see us reach this harmony. We have chosen a path that respects our history, our people, and our constraints. Let us cast our votes for Proposal D with confidence and a peaceful heart.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'll vote for Proposal D too. It seems like the safest choice for everyone, and I hope the costs stay manageable. I'm glad we could all agree.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm voting for Proposal D! It's the only one that can beat the signal ghosts and actually help the people working at the plants! This was such a fun mystery to solve! Hehe!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will vote for Proposal D. While it does not address the data inconsistencies I highlighted, it is the only viable option that satisfies the constraints of our infrastructure and staffing. Logic dictates we choose the sustainable tool.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will also vote for Proposal D. It is the only option that provides a practical solution without imposing an unsustainable administrative burden on our exhausted staff. It is the most responsible choice.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
